```sql
CREATE TABLE nullable_pair(person TEXT, day TEXT, UNIQUE(person,day));
INSERT INTO nullable_pair VALUES('Mira',NULL),('Mira',NULL);
SELECT person,day
FROM nullable_pair
ORDER BY rowid;
```
Both rows are accepted. UNIQUE does not treat the two missing day values as the same known value. rowid is SQLite’s internal integer row identifier for this ordinary table; it supplies a deterministic display order here.

