```sql
CREATE TABLE notes(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,score INTEGER);
INSERT INTO notes VALUES(1,10),(2,10),(3,8),(4,8),(5,5);
SELECT id,score
FROM notes
ORDER BY score DESC,id ASC
LIMIT 2
OFFSET 2;
```
The full ID order is 1,2,3,4,5. Skipping two and taking two returns IDs 3 and 4.

```sql
CREATE TABLE notes(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,score INTEGER);
INSERT INTO notes VALUES(1,10),(2,10),(3,8),(4,8),(5,5);
SELECT id,score
FROM notes
ORDER BY score DESC,id ASC
LIMIT 2
OFFSET 4;
```
Skipping four leaves only ID 5. LIMIT is a maximum, not a requirement to fill every page.

```sql
CREATE TABLE results(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,name TEXT,score INTEGER);
INSERT INTO results VALUES(1,'Mira',9),(2,'Oren',9),(3,'Paz',7),(4,'Rin',5);
SELECT id,name,score,ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY score DESC,id) AS position,DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY score DESC) AS level
FROM results
ORDER BY score DESC,id;
```
Positions are 1,2,3,4. Dense ranks are 1,1,2,3: the two scores of 9 share rank 1.

